<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador's Alarcon completes new cabinet.</title>
<headline>Ecuador's Alarcon completes new cabinet.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO, Ecuador 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuadoran President Fabian Alarcon, head of an interim 18-month administration after Congress ousted president Abdala Bucaram three weeks ago, completed his new cabinet Thursday after appointing his Agriculture and Environment ministers, officials said.</p>
<p>The cabinet is conformed as follows:</p>
<p>Vice President, Rosalia Arteaga</p>
<p>Government Minister, Cesar Verduga</p>
<p>Foreign Minister, Jose Ayala</p>
<p>Defense Minister, Ramiro Ricaurte</p>
<p>Finance Minister, Carlos Davalos</p>
<p>Public Works Minister, Estuardo Hidalgo</p>
<p>Education Minister, Mario Jaramillo</p>
<p>Labor Minister, Edgar Ribadeneira</p>
<p>Public Health Minister, Guillermo Wagner</p>
<p>Social Welfare Minister, Gonzalo Baquero</p>
<p>Agriculture Minister, Alfredo Saltos</p>
<p>Industry Minister, Benigno Sotomayor</p>
<p>Tourism Minister, Juana Vallejo</p>
<p>Energy Minister, Raul Baca</p>
<p>Environment Minister, Flor de Maria Vidal</p>
<p>Housing and Urban Development Minister, Diego Ponce</p>
<p>Administration Secretary, Arturo Gangotena</p>
<p>Monetary Board President, Danilo Carrera</p>
<p>Central Bank Manager, Fidel Jaramillo</p>
<p>(( -- Quito Newsroom 5932 258433))</p>
